<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<part xml:id="num-strand" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Number</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>
      Number is the foundation of all mathematics. This strand covers the number systems used in Junior Cycle — natural numbers, integers, and rationals — along with the operations, properties, and applications built on them.
    </p>
    <p>
      Topics include place value, operations, factors and primes, fractions, decimals, percentages, ratio, indices, standard form, estimation, measurement, and financial mathematics.
    </p>
  </introduction>

